<!--
  SCENARIO TESTS, NOT UNIT TESTS. Every case here needs external inputs (the
  stock DOS 3.3 System Master, which is fetched rather than committed) and a
  booted guest executing real 6502 code. They live in their own DLL so they
  cannot run in the unit-test suite by accident: CI names UnitTest.dll only,
  and the one deliberate way to run these is `scripts/RunTests.ps1 -Scenario`.

  The shared guest-driving helpers (GuestSession, HeadlessHost, MachineIdle,
  the scraper and the injector) compile into BOTH this DLL and UnitTest.dll;
  the two are separate modules, so the duplication costs nothing at link time
  and keeps one copy of the paging rules in the source tree.
-->
